<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Plog (255)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>plog &lt;player&gt;
</pre>
<p>Starts logging a player's commands, or stops it if they are already 
logged: the same command does both. Every command typed around them, by 
them and by anyone else whose commands reach them, goes into a file 
named &lt;player&gt;watchdog in the server's log directory, one line each: who 
typed it, the command and its arguments.
</p><p>Use it to gather evidence of cheating or abuse. It works on players 
anywhere in the game of a lower level than yours. The player isn't told. 
It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Snoop</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Snoop</a>
</pre>




</div>